cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Voice Agent Evaluation Corpus and the TRG Reporting Standard"
message: "If you use this corpus or the TRG standard, please cite it."
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Negi
    given-names: Shivam
    email: negi.sh@northeastern.edu
    affiliation: Northeastern University
abstract: >-
  A verified metadata corpus of 41 sources on real-time voice agents,
  covering end-to-end speech-to-speech architectures, cascaded pipelines,
  turn-taking and voice activity projection, conversational benchmarks,
  agentic evaluation, and streaming synthesis. Ships metadata and SHA-256
  hashes rather than PDFs, so the corpus is auditable without redistributing
  copyrighted material. Includes TRG (Timing-Recovery-Grounded), a minimum
  reporting standard for real-time voice agent evaluation, with a fillable
  template and a compliance validator.
keywords:
  - voice agents
  - spoken dialogue systems
  - full-duplex dialogue
  - evaluation methodology
  - benchmarking
  - turn-taking
  - speech-to-speech
